// Status list service (ADR-018, ADR-019). One package serves both the W3C
// Bitstring Status List and the IETF Token Status List. The two kinds
// share allocation, storage, and key management. They differ only in the
// encoding and the signing envelope (ADR-019 decision 4).
// The public list endpoints are standard HTTP GET handlers, not RPCs
// (ADR-003 decision 7). They send cache headers and an ETag:
// Each service serves its lists at one path, so the path holds no kind:
//   GET /status/{list_id} on the bitstring service serves the VCDM 2.0
//   list credential.
//   GET /status/{list_id} on the token service serves
//   application/statuslist+jwt.
//   GET /status/{list_id} on the token service with Accept
//   application/statuslist+cwt serves the CWT.
//   GET /.well-known/jwks.json serves the signing keys.

